  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections - Delaware County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n Delaware County\n Iowa • Elections\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Delaware County\nElections\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \nWelcome to the Delaware County Elections Website\n The Auditor’s Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find past or upcoming election information.\n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \nWhere Do I Vote?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nAm I Registered?\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nElected Officials\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n3\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election\n General Election\n \n\n Election Information Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJul\n \n21\n \n \n\n 2026 Lake Delhi Trustee Election\n Special Election\n \n\n Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJun\n \n2\n \n \n\n 2026 Primary Election\n Primary Election\n \n\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n News\n \n\n 2021 Election Law Changes for Iowa Voters\n \n October 8, 2021 View a list of important changes to Iowa election law passed by the 2021 Iowa legislature. These changes are effective immediately. \n\n\n\nAll News\n \n \n\n \n FAQ\n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nWhat is Voter ID?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nStarting in 2019, voters must provide an ID when going to vote. Pre-Registered voters who do not have an acceptable form of ID will be allowed to cast a provisional ballot. Election Day registrants who do not have an acceptable form of ID will be allowed to either cast a provisional ballot or have another registered voter from your precinct may attest to their identification. Learn more about provisional ballots and attesting on our Voter ID page. \n \n\nThere are 6 approved types of identification that may be used: \n \n \n \nan Iowa Driver’s License or Non-Operator ID \n \na Voter ID issued by the Secretary of State or the Auditor’s Office \n \na current US Passport \n \na US Military ID \n \na US Veteran’s ID \n \na Tribal ID \n \n\n \n\n \n \nAll Frequently Asked Questions\n \n \n\n \n Delaware County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated October 1, 2026\n \n\n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n5,369\n \n\n \nNo Party \n \n\n\n \n4,641\n \n\n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n2,203\n \n\n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n65\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 12,278\n \n Register to Vote\n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Delaware County, Iowa, Elections website at https://delawarecountyelections.iowa.gov.\n\n\n \n\n Delaware County Courthouse\n\n 301 E Main St, Manchester, IA 52057\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Delaware County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n Monday - Friday \n \n8:00 AM - 4:30 PM \n \nContact Numbers\n\n Phone: (563) 927-4701\n \nFax: (563) 927-6423 \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n"
